{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed for review: change 1702 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1702 (commit 6faf9c3440, rebased onto ae6f2ac57a).\n\nFull CI pytest on the rebased tree: 12621 passed, 52 skipped, 3 errors. All three errors were the SAME artifact of my own tooling, not the change: 'Test moved the repo HEAD (ee204e2188 -> 6faf9c3440)' — the repo-commit guard fired because I amended the commit (a comment re-wrap) while the suite was still running, so tests that assert HEAD stability saw it move under them. Re-ran all three affected modules against the now-stable HEAD: 74 passed, HEAD unchanged before and after. Lesson recorded for myself: do not amend while a suite is in flight.\n\nGate set, final tree: 15/15 scripts/check_*.py; complexity baseline active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0; module-size 0 violations against the 800 cap; make lint and make typecheck clean (518 files); all five generators re-run with zero diff; wall-clock-assert, raw-git-write and comment-hygiene gates clean. verify-commit-ticket resolves the trailer to this ticket; committed and signed off as RebarBotNava <joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com>.\n\nWaiting on LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before submit."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786598973306652001,"uuid":"b54c3626-1b47-4d7a-92a6-3c73a3c5f203"}